+# Non-authorizing historical logical-Dev evidence contract
+
+This implements only the common evidence layer under protocol0e4ce396. No validation/N26 integration, authority, budget amendment, source integration or online release is implied. Every271 existing6f source file stays byte-identical. Added code is one metadata adapter plus focused synthetic tests and this contract/protocol. All real inputs remain closed during CPU preparation.
+
+## Runtime ownership and source
+
+Run the future adapter only after the continuation closes, its controller dies and root independently reviews the immutable terminal under6f. Then root may integrate these additive files into the owning study. `ROOT` must resolve to the approved `study_worktree`; the continuation control directory must be its parent/variants/n25_actuator_clipped_rbf/infrastructure-continuation-v1. The imported c/e/terminal/bridge/worker/report modules must resolve to owning scripts. `c.rows(seal)` reads the fixed `c.SEAL` path: the inventory's seal must be that same resolved file. Production does not replace globals or clone functions. Synthetic tests bind isolated fixture paths through ordinary monkeypatch fixtures only.
+
+Historical source records remain5a(257) and6f(271), irrespective of current HEAD. Immutable Git objects are separately allowlisted: bootstrap only6f's tracked original-source-v1.json; then exact257+271 paths. Every object is hash-checked,16MiB/file and128MiB total.255 files and exact two-file/four-function whole-byte reverse bridge are verified. The currently reused eight continuation modules, original N25 contract/report/backend/reference/UUID helper remain identical to6f. The backend contract must be the same original-contract module as c.old, and contract/reference/UUID imports must resolve to owning scripts. The worker's four pure metadata primitives are AST-byte-bound, allowing a future separately reviewed administrative route insertion without pretending old HEAD is current. Actual numerical arithmetic is never executed. Root must separately approve every future downstream source delta.
+
+## Input envelope and bounds
+
+```
+{
+ schema: "n25-logical-dev-evidence-input-v1",
+ root_authorized: true,
+ owning_root: "/.../research_sessions/.../study_worktree",
+ files: [{path: absolute, sha256: exact}, ...],
+ references: {
+  old_source, source, seal, seal_review, source_bridge, source_review,
+  authority, release, plan, status, result, root_review, controller,
+  journal_projection, resource_projection
+ }
+}
+```
+
+The15 reference names are exact, each a path/SHA pair. A disabled template has root_authorized=false and unresolved values. Metadata inventory is max512 unique resolved paths,16MiB/file,128MiB distinct bytes; size is checked before bounded read. Source objects and helper/protocol bytes are a separate explicit static-source scope. Existing Reader caches inventoried metadata. The old backend JSON validator additionally rehashes its one fixed, explicitly inventoried historical plan; it follows no tensor or other variable payload ref. Its original metadata gate/source stays unchanged.
+
+Inventory closure includes historical manifests; seal and its declared metadata refs; original plan/result/root review/status/Dev-only snapshot/source review/authority/budget/runtime JSON; continuation bridge/review/authority/release/plan/status/result/controller/independent root review and Dev-only snapshot; each new accepted terminal/context/receipt/audit/process/audit-start; historical resource proof/plan/report/process/terminal; and the two new root projections. Historical receipt evidence.files are canonical metadata only, never opened. No images, tensor/native event index, raw Stage records, model files or protected outcome records are authorized. Raw stage_events.jsonl/stage_responses.jsonl/events.jsonl and the full private attempt-ledger.jsonl/gpu-healthcheck-ledger.jsonl are explicitly rejected in the metadata inventory. Root must review all metadata roles; arbitrary extra files cannot acquire a read role by being listed.
+
+No sealer is rerun, no old result is repaired, and no current-HEAD old validator/report writer/outcome validator/evidence_record/native replay is called. Pure6f terminal.review_existing is reused with the historical6f source explicitly. Metadata acceptance remains reliance on original metered native audits plus root attestations; it is not a new native numerical/safety audit.
+
+## Root projection clarification
+
+Root message of2026-10-01 expressly narrowed current-journal handling to root-attested projections. Both are frozen only after immutable terminal and independent root review:
+
+- `n25-current-dev-journal-projection-v1`: original_events, continuation_events, original_event_count, continuation_event_count.
+- `n25-current-resource-projection-v1`: resource_id, resource_kind, events, event_count. Include ALL events matching the original N25 resource ID OR its fixed resource kind, so another reservation of that opportunity cannot be omitted.
+
+Both also require root_terminal_review ref; source_ledger and collector path/SHA refs; collected_at nonempty timestamp; all_matching_events_included=true; protected_events_included=false. Source ledger and collector refs are provenance attestations and NEVER followed. Collection time is descriptive; elapsed time is not a freshness proof.
+
+The adapter compares the Dev projections to old/new snapshots and original resource settlement. `check_current_matching_events(projection, events, resource_projection, resources)` is a pure function requiring caller-filtered current matching events. Future downstream release/admission MUST invoke it using the normal runner's already-read journal: ONLY the two named Dev cohorts and resource ID/kind. It rejects later or changed matching events and foreign/protected rows supplied accidentally. It does NOT require the complete old private ledger SHA to stay unchanged as unrelated legitimate cohorts append. Root refresh/current-subset checking is mandatory; this common task adds no runner hook or dispatch authority.
+
+## Scientific/evidence semantics
+
+Only complete valid logical promotion, complete valid rejection or valid whole-original-quadruple numerical futility can create evidence. Original INVALID alone, a new invalidity, missing independent root review, active controller, status/journal mismatch, late original audit, extra reservation or malformed/missing lineage blocks creation. All18 imported identities/refs and original Unknowns remain; new indices18..39 stay ordered, with only index18 the named recovery. All accepted new calls have complete normal telemetry/native receipts. Combined dispatched is accepted scientific cells+1; imports have no new charge.
+
+All19 original costs and six unknown-token calls are retained. Old/new/combined observed costs are independently recomputed; missing values remain missing and totals remain partial. Neither old native/safety Unknowns nor UNPROVEN API-only attribution becomes true. The original5a resource proof is checked against its original source/runtime/plan/report/process/terminal and exactly one settled reserved→dispatched→completed group. The unchanged existing JSON report checker verifies its12 cases/identity/coverage; no actual tensor operation or new proof occurs. Historical GPU resource time is reported separately and is not an episode charge.
+
+The actual continuation root schema carries an inline source record and no native field; native summaries come from the result. All root/result/status/source/proof refs and actual present fields are bound. New status contains new22-prefix keys, attempts and outcomes; logical accepted mapping includes old18. The root cleanup snapshot remains historical, while fresh public process/boot/tick/group checks are repeated. No process is signalled.
+
+Output schema n25-logical-dev-evidence-v1 includes logical_disposition/counts/mapping/native/auxiliary, unique attempt IDs, old/new/combined cost coverage, historical Unknowns, all provenance refs, original/continuation source records, settled resource cost and reader ref. It ALWAYS has allow_validation=false, allow_n26=false, gpu_authorized=false. It also declares current_matching_event_check_required_at_release=true, projections_are_root_attestations=true and underlying_full_ledger_refs_followed=false. Distinct future callers—not this record—must implement the mutually exclusive validation promotion and N26 valid-rejection gates under separate root-reviewed protocols.
+
+## Deferred root invocation
+
+1. Keep live6f unchanged through closure and original independent terminal review. Review this CPU source/guard/tests and additive source manifest; freeze a NEW root-authorized bounded inventory and two current projections. No actual record is created during executor preparation.
+2. After source integration is separately approved, ensure controller dead and acquire the existing controller/runner ownership locks in the root orchestration. Call the adapter from owning study, with CUDA invisible and two CPU threads:
+
+```
+CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' OMP_NUM_THREADS=2 MKL_NUM_THREADS=2 OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=2 PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 \
+/home/hynx/miniconda3/envs/vla-pilot/bin/python -B \
+W/scripts/qd_ed_n25_cont_downstream.py --input ROOT_AUTHORIZED_METADATA_INPUT \
+--output N25/infrastructure-continuation-v1/logical-dev-evidence-v1.json
+```
+
+The CLI accepts only a new output below that control directory, never overwrites a result/seal. It imports no adjacent implementation module: owning path checks enforce this. `python scripts/...py` supplies scripts/ for legacy absolute imports; any root import helper must supply the same scripts/ path explicitly. If the controller execution directory is needed for lock acquisition, create only that authorized parent first. This is directory preparation, not a new episode.
+3. Independently review the generated non-authorizing evidence. A later separately reviewed caller supplies the current filtered subset check and its own source/proof/capacity/fresh-cohort/authority/release gates. Common evidence neither transfers continuation hours nor modifies494/100 limits or any protected reserve.
+
+No actual terminal, projection, proof, private state or protected input was opened by the CPU executor. Actual Git-object and real-metadata review remains root work; tests use an explicit fake Git object reader and synthetic metadata only.
