+
+Reuse unchanged6f terminal.review_existing and metadata helpers with historical6f source passed explicitly; do not invoke terminal.main, report writer/analyze, runtime/current-HEAD validator, outcome/native auditor, evidence_record, model, simulator or new arithmetic. Do not monkeypatch globals in production or clone the independent terminal reader. Existing c.rows depends on c.SEAL; enforce the same approved owning-study path, and document this actual dependency. Production source-path aliases must resolve consistently; synthetic tests may bind fixture paths through normal test fixtures. If reuse requires an existing-source edit, stop implementation and report the exact reason for root review first.
+
+Verify historical5a257 and6f271 source manifests against immutable Git object bytes, with exact canonical digests and a closed list. Verify the historical255 unchanged files and two-file/four-function reverse bridge using those bytes; never relabel historical backend proof as newly generated. Verify the actual reader and helpers remain identical to6f. Root attestations and metadata digests remain attestations, not new numerical audit. Do not require missing native/safety gates of the original invalid attempt to become true. Keep its literal terminal, all19 old costs, six unknown-token calls, late-audit absences and UNPROVEN API-only attribution. No old outcome or result rewriting.
+
+The common record must remain non-authorizing: schema n25-logical-dev-evidence-v1, explicit allow_validation=false, allow_n26=false, gpu_authorized=false. Include root-reviewed provenance, independently recomputed logical disposition/counts/ordered accepted mapping and old/new/combined cost coverage. Distinct downstream callers will later grant exactly one gate. It may produce evidence only for complete valid logical promotion, complete valid rejection, or valid whole-quad futility. Original INVALID alone, new invalidity, status disagreement, later reservation, active controller, missing independent terminal review or malformed proof/metadata rejects evidence creation. For valid closure all new dispatched cells have normal accepted receipts, combined dispatched=accepted scientific cells+1, original imports consume no new budget. Recompute exact-once old/new/combined observed costs and preserve unknowns; do not silently use claimed convenience totals. Bind all status/cohort/source/plan/ordered new-key fields and root-review fields actually present in their schemas. Do not invent native fields in the root review, which obtains native summaries via its immutable result.
+
+Require original and continuation journal subsets equal their frozen snapshots with no unsettled or later reservation; only these Dev cohorts are inspected. Verify original resource proof settlement from the existing health ledger metadata and its historical plan/report/process/terminal; no new proof execution. Public process identity/boot/ticks/owned descendants checks use existing helper, no signalling. Actual metadata record creation is deferred until root explicitly reviews the final CPU delivery and the real continuation has closed and passed independent review.
+
+CPU tests use only synthetic bounded fixtures plus allowed static source/protocols. Enforce no GPU/API/network/subprocess dispatch, no real history/protected payload access, two CPU threads, CUDA uninitialized. A test-only explicit fake Git object reader may cover source closure; actual Git source verification is root work after CPU acceptance. Meaningful tests: three admissible dispositions and mutually exclusive future gate interpretation; all invalid/missing/live/status discrepancies; exact18 imported mapping/named retry/duplicate costs/extra or omitted new cells; inline-vs-ref source shape and actual root schema; old six unknowns retained/new incomplete usage rejected; no tensor/raw Stage/current-validator fallback; historical source/reverse bridge drift; wrong proof or unsettled resource cost; late original audit; root inventory cap/hash/unknown file rejection. Failures and corrections remain in logs. No blanket retesting of unchanged scientific modules.
+
